 "about": {
  "text": "Robert Kramer is one of the most versatile American directors of the 20th century. His body of work, created between 1965 and 1999, in which documentary and fiction, film and video, the personal and the political blend together, has recently gained renewed attention through international retrospectives. Kramer was a founding member of the militant collective Newsreel in 1967; his early films chronicle the political struggles of the radical left around 1968. In *ICE* (1969), *MILESTONES* (1975), and *ROUTE ONE/USA* (1989), he offered a lucid portrayal of the contradictory and violent history and present of his homeland. Between 1979 and his untimely death in 1999, Kramer lived in France and incorporated many of the essayistic impulses of European cinema into his films.",
  "lang": "en",
